      "blockId": "tour:lead:e3456bc1f4d270f4",
      "field": "lead",
      "sourceTextSha256": "dc4a1d619cbe843f0f7f50d744baec773a7807fd5af1b0809af163cd4551d549",
      "text": "Eight days connect Mexico City with the Maya heritage of the Yucatán. After the Anthropology Museum, the pyramids of Teotihuacan and a boat trip through Xochimilco, you fly to Mérida. From there, your route takes you to Uxmal, Kabah, the Santa Bárbara cenotes and Chichén Itzá, before ending on the Caribbean coast. Seven hotel nights and tours in English and Spanish are included; the domestic flight is payable separately.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "model": "GPT-6",
        "runId": "ada_en_1f8e8fe01ca4_20261104",
        "wordAbsenceReason": "The verified Word 2027 contains the daily itinerary but no single introductory overview corresponding to this RU lead; translated the current RU summary."
      }
    },
